# Workspace Auth Isolation (QicTrader)

This workspace must **never** change the Mac-global GitHub or Heroku CLI login.
JP uses many other projects on the same machine; `gh auth switch` and
`heroku login` log him out of those.

## Forbidden (global identity changes)

Do **not** run any of these in this workspace:

- `gh auth switch`
- `gh auth login`
- `gh auth logout`
- `heroku login`
- `heroku auth:login`
- `heroku auth:logout`
- `heroku accounts:set`
- `heroku accounts:add`

## Required instead

Before any `gh`, `git push`/`git pull` to GitHub, or `heroku` command:

```bash
source ~/.qictrader-secrets/load-all.sh
```

That sets `GH_TOKEN` and `HEROKU_API_KEY` for **this shell only**. Those env
vars override the global CLI identity without touching the keyring or other
workspaces.

If `load-all.sh` or the token files are missing, **stop and tell JP** to
complete `ops/workspace-auth.md` setup. Do not fall back to `gh auth switch`.

## Trello

Trello already follows this pattern via `~/.qictrader-secrets/trello.env`.
Keep using that. Never paste key/token into commands or chat.

## Why

`GH_TOKEN` / `HEROKU_API_KEY` are process-scoped. `gh auth switch` is
machine-scoped. Only the first is safe in a multi-project setup.
